  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Added `patch_shape.rs` (`PatchShape`, `classify_patch`) and `names.rs` (`build_feature_names`, `FeatureNames`, `NameKind`, `NameInputs`) under `crates/geometry/src/geometry/feature/` to name every pickable feature deterministically in local space (`Face N`, `Bore N`, `Cylinder N`, `Curved face N`, `Edge N`, `Vertex N`).\n- Exposed `singleton_chain_id_with_lattice` in `crates/geometry/src/geometry/feature.rs` so remaining singleton edges join the shared edge numbering.\n- Added `FeatureNamesMemo` in `crates/app/src/schema.rs` and `crates/app/src/pick/names.rs` (`feature_names_of`, `feature_name`, `feature_name_or_kind`, `label_in_table`, `geo_label`) to cache the table per entity revision and live `Arc<[Triangle]>` allocation on both models and stocks.\n- Updated `Display for FeatureSel` in `crates/app/src/operation/types/sel.rs` to print plain nouns (`face`, `edge`, `curved face`, `vertex`) with no `{id:#x}` digest.\n- Updated `crates/app` pick helpers, `fixture_locate.rs`, `fixture_locate_land.rs`, operation geometry/selection/boundary refusals, and MCP handlers (`list_features`, `detect_pockets` `floor_name`, `get_operation_geometry`, `set_operation_geometry`, `set_operation_area`, `set_wcs_from_features`, `get_selection`) to read from the shared table while keeping 64-bit hashes on `GeoSel`/`FeatureSel` and MCP `\"id\"`.\n- Removed `short_id` hex truncation from `crates/ui/src/state.rs` and routed Setup, WCS, Orient, Plane, Points, Locate, Boundary, Edge, Origin, Cylinder, Vertex pick rows, status lines, and Geometry chips through `pick::geo_label`.\n- Added design notes in `docs/decisions/2403-shared-pick-names.md`.\n\n## Before / after pick labels\n\nThe same top face of the same `part` box is selected in both component captures. Each image shows the production WCS row above the production Geometry selection chips. Before uses the previous WCS, feature-display, and chip implementations; after uses PR head `f6f4027138aa25f21eafcc2ab75a4346319dae8e`.\n\nThese are offscreen egui widget captures, software-rasterized from egui's actual tessellated paint output and font atlas because this machine has no graphics adapter. They are component evidence, not desktop viewport captures. The temporary capture harness is not committed.\n\nBefore: WCS shows `face 0x4839531e1edd1cf4 of 'part'`; Geometry shows `Face part`.\n\n![Before: WCS row and Geometry chip for the same picked top face](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/db5a66930b262ba2dea1114efde54122d829d7fb/2484/pick-labels-before.png)\n\nAfter: both WCS and Geometry show `Face 6 of 'part'`.\n\n![After: WCS row and Geometry chip share the picked face name](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/db5a66930b262ba2dea1114efde54122d829d7fb/2484/pick-labels-after.png)\n\nImages are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch, commit `db5a66930b262ba2dea1114efde54122d829d7fb`.\n\n## Cause\n\n`Display for FeatureSel` formatted internal 64-bit ids (`face 0x...`, `welded face 0x...`) directly into user messages, `crates/ui/src/state.rs::short_id` rendered truncated hex ids on missing chips, and pick UI rows (`locate_pick`, `wcs_pick`, `setup_orient_pick`, status lines) built inconsistent per-caller strings without a shared model/stock name table.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pinning test `mcp_and_app_refusals_use_shared_friendly_pick_names_without_hex` (`crates/app/tests/mcp_pick.rs`) failed on `upstream/main` (`list_features item must include friendly 'name'`) and passes after the fix (`mcp_pick` 8/8, `mcp_live` 14/14, `fixture_locate_stock_cylinder` 3/3, `winding_align` 9/9).\n- Pinning test `egui_app::wcs_pick_tests::picked_items_never_show_hex_ids_and_keep_one_name_across_pages` failed on `upstream/main` (`status leaked hex id: Setup1: face 0x4839531e1edd1cf4 of 'part' picked as Z`) and passes after the fix (`camcraft-ui --test operations` 31/31; `camcraft-geometry` `feature::names` 2/2; `camcraft-app` `pick::names::tests::feature_names_cache_once_per_revision_for_model_and_stock` passes).\n- Mutation checks:\n  1. Reverted `Display for FeatureSel` in `crates/app/src/operation/types/sel.rs` to `{id:#x}` -> `mcp_and_app_refusals_use_shared_friendly_pick_names_without_hex` failed (`FeatureSel::Display leaked hex: face 0x885acc12`), then passed after restore.\n  2. Bypassed the `FeatureNamesMemo` hit check in `crates/app/src/pick/names.rs` -> `feature_names_cache_once_per_revision_for_model_and_stock` failed (`left: 2, right: 1`), then passed after restore.\n  3. Reverted `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_pick_row.rs` to `\"{} of '{}' sets {}\"` -> `picked_items_never_show_hex_ids_and_keep_one_name_across_pages` failed on WCS vs chip name equality, then passed after restore.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed cleanly after all edits.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main --only app --only ui --only clippy` passed 550 of 551 steps (including all `ui` suites with `trace_parity` and `clippy -D warnings`); only the known slow baseline test `app::shoulder_adaptive::containment_outside_clears_past_the_edge_never_the_recess` (>60s in debug) failed, as noted on the issue. An earlier `gate quick --base upstream/main` run before server restart also passed all `geometry`, `kernel`, `cl`, `tools`, `post`, `sim`, and `motion` suites (steps 01..305).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone (`0` `.nc` or `.cl` files changed relative to branch base `c0c92ee86`).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `--release -- --ignored` heavy lanes and Windows UI pixel snapshots on Linux.\n- Interactive desktop viewport rendering outside headless `egui_kittest` and `trace_parity`.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nTouches different functions or symbols in files also edited by open PRs: `#2448` (`crates/ui/src/state.rs`), `#2370` (`crates/ui/src/state.rs`), `#2092` (`crates/app/src/schema.rs`), `#2253` (`crates/app/src/schema.rs`, `crates/ui/src/state.rs`, `crates/ui/tests/operations.rs`), `#2134` (`crates/app/src/commands/operation/geometry.rs`, `crates/app/src/schema.rs`), `#2185` (`crates/ui/src/state.rs`), `#1798` (`crates/ui/src/state.rs`), `#2256` (`feature.rs`, `selection.rs`, `feature_sel.rs`, `edge_pick.rs`, `interact.rs`, `state.rs`), `#2433` (`selection.rs`), and stacked `#2149` (`mcp/area.rs`, `boundary_draft.rs`, `state.rs`). Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Show one shared, cached user-friendly name for each picked face, bore, cylinder, curved face, edge, and vertex instead of hexadecimal IDs.\n\nFixes #2403\n\n",
